<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Jose, California</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Jose is a city in the Santa Clara Valley of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, founded in 1777 as San José de Guadalupe, the first civilian town (pueblo) of Spanish Alta California. It was briefly the state capital after California joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1850. Since the late 20th century it has been the largest city of Silicon Valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-jose-california.jpg" alt="San Jose, California" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Payton Chung · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valencia_Hotel,_Santana_Row_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
